      "html_url": "https://github.com/WTFitsmemyself",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/WTFitsmemyself/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/WTFitsmemyself/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/WTFitsmemyself/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/WTFitsmemyself/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/WTFitsmemyself/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/WTFitsmemyself/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/WTFitsmemyself/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/WTFitsmemyself/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/WTFitsmemyself/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "When -listenonion=1 (default) and -bind is specified without =onion, the automatic Tor hidden service routes incoming Tor connections through the first -bind address instead of creating a dedicated Tor socket (127.0.0.1:8334=onion). This causes -netinfo and getnetworkinfo to miscount Tor connections as regular IPv4/IPv6 connections.\n\nAdd a warning to the -bind help text and to doc/tor.md explaining that users should include =onion on at least one -bind address when using -bind with automatic Tor hidden service creation.",
