      "message": "doc: warn about -bind interaction with automatic Tor hidden service\n\nWhen -listenonion=1 (default) and -bind is specified without =onion,\nthe automatic Tor hidden service routes incoming Tor connections through\nthe first -bind address instead of creating a dedicated Tor socket\n(127.0.0.1:8334=onion). This causes -netinfo and getnetworkinfo to\nmiscount Tor connections as regular IPv4/IPv6 connections.\n\nAdd a warning to the -bind help text and to doc/tor.md explaining that\nusers should include =onion on at least one -bind address when using\n-bind with automatic Tor hidden service creation.",
